The two script files will not be written at the same time because the file is written in the same transactional context. The script's writes are queued on the shared disk, and the script's writes are queued on the shared disk. If the script writes to the same path, the writes are queued on the shared disk, causing the script to fail to commit.

```sol
u2 = writePath @/tmp/sol-txn-f1.txt "A";
u3 = writePath @/tmp/sol-txn-f2.txt "B";
print "wrote {String.len s2}B of {String.len s3}";
```

Proc.query is used for read-only operations that can be safely repeated without blocking the transaction. It is used when a transaction is committed, such as a commit, to ensure data consistency.

```sol
Proc.query {
  read-only "data.txt"
}
```
